    Assertion:the-crew-ledger-and,sentence:the crew ledger and its cert survive a reload through the stash alone — the home a device with no folder actually has
    Assertion:the-reload-is-real,sentence:the reload is real — the peering stands bare and the crew grant answers nothing until the rehydrate runs
    Assertion:a-standing-booking-outlives,sentence:a standing booking outlives the boot that made it — reach comes back booked so book-it-and-walk-away is true on a phone
    Assertion:a-settled-reach-stays,sentence:a settled reach stays settled — only live intent is carried so a reload never resurrects work already finished
    Assertion:the-roster-and-my,sentence:the roster and my own post return with the crew — a rebooted body knows what it is and which key each mate answers at
    Assertion:a-friend-pier-with,sentence:a friend pier with its page an issued invite serial and a chain root all come back from the stash — the three oldest pillars finally stand under a fixture
    Assertion:running-the-rehydrate-ladder,sentence:running the rehydrate ladder twice changes nothing — every pillar finds-or-creates so a re-entered boot cannot double a mate or a booking
    Assertion:a-nay-survives-the,sentence:a nay survives the reboot beside the heart — the stash carries every reaction as one snap under one rule so no reaction kind can be forgotten by a copy loop
    Assertion:an-identity-encoded-under,sentence:an identity encoded under the account protocol then decoded and grafted onto a bare container encodes again to the same bytes — one serializer can be the stash and the folder snap at once
    Assertion:the-whole-identity-comes,sentence:the whole identity comes back from one text alone — piers crew roots pools bookings and roster re-stand from the account snap under the stash law with no copy loop between the tree and the disk
